{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533554-bloodlines-2-clan-highlight-tremere","id":1533554,"title":"Bloodlines 2 - Clan Highlight Tremere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-04T02:10:29-07:00","id":1533554,"title":"Bloodlines 2 - Clan Highlight Tremere","content":"More details on <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/clan-highlight-tremere\" target=\"_blank\">playing Clan Tremere in Bloodlines 2 have been revealed</a>.<br /> <br /> Here's the ability-list:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Corrosive Touch<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Passive:</b> Bodies will dissolve away after being fed on.<br /> <br /> Cauldron of Blood<br /> <br /> Torture your victim by boiling their blood slowly from the inside, making them drop to their knees screaming. Nearby enemies/civilians are drawn to their screams.<br /> <br /> Recall<br /> <br /> First Use: Mark your current location with a ward.<br /> <br /> Second Use: Deconstruct yourself, and explosively reconstruct yourself at the marked location obliterating any enemies standing in that spot.<br /> <br /> Blood Curse<br /> <br /> Curse a victim. The next time they take damage, their body swells horrifically and they explode, doing damage to all around them.<br /> <br /> Blood Salvo<br /> <br /> Conjure a set of blood daggers that can be thrown at enemies.<br /> <br /> Greed<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Perk:</b> A chance when feeding, that the last used ability receives twice as much blood, increasing the rate you can perform abilities. </div> </div> </div>The abilities sound more fun to use but the Clan Passive is a weird choice for Clan Tremere. Not just that but it's clearly a stealth-focused passive. Wouldn't have thought they would lean into that for Tremere gameplay. Also makes me wonder how they're gonna portray this &quot;Corrosive Touch&quot;.<br /> <br /> In general, it's a bit disappointing that like with the Brujah-highlight there's no video this time around either. With the Brujah-one I could kind of understand it because the extended gameplay-reveal already showed off some of the Brujah-abilities. But that the Tremere-reveal doesn't come with a video either to show off the abilities in action is... concerning. Well, hopefully, they will at least have a video for the Ventrue-reveal in... I guess, it will be late May when that happens. Because otherwise that would mean we would see the Ventrue-abilities only in action once the game has been released.<br /> <br /> And still, there's no showcasing of any roleplaying-elements/systems. Just that you will have various NPCs that give you access to the Abilities from all the other Clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T10:23:59-07:00","id":1533706,"title":"","content":"I think this makes a nice companion-piece for the latest Bloodlines 2 reveal:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PGhi7MLKbj4\" data-code=\"PGhi7MLKbj4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/PGhi7MLKbj4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> The tl;dr is that Paradox sucks as a publisher and the last few years have been a history of failures. Most importantly from the rumors Bellular in that video hears as a fellow game-developer, they agree on a release date with the developers and then force them to release the game <i>no matter what</i>. Doesn't matter what state the game is in. And this has led to bad to mediocre game-releases time and time again over the last couple of years. But it doesn't seem like they're course-correcting. The pattern has just been repeating itself time and time again.<br /> <br /> And to add my personal commentary here: Bloodlines 2 would fit perfectly into this pattern. It's just yet another rushed release that Paradox as a publisher enforced that ends up being bad to mediocre. And if it's too bad, they will yank their support immediately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}